# Bree to Rivendell

**Description:** The Flight to the Ford. Escape the Nazgul and find refuge in the Last Homely House.
**Category:** Middle-earth
**Color:** #0000FF
**Character:** Aragorn
**ID:** rivendell

---

## Waypoints

### Bree
📍 -38.700, 175.700
📏 52000m

You lead the four hobbits out of the East-gate before dawn, leaving a stuffed decoy behind at the Prancing Pony. Bill the pony carries the supplies. The road is empty and the land grows wild.

---

### Midgewater Marshes
📍 -39.050, 176.100
📏 53500m

Neeker-breekers and midges haunt the stagnant pools. Three days of misery through sucking bog, never quite sure of the path. But it keeps you off the main road, and for now that's what matters.

---

### Weathertop
📍 -39.450, 176.450
📏 56000m

Amon Sûl, the ancient watchtower. You make camp in the ruined dell below the summit. In the dead of night five Nazgûl come, tall shadows robed in black. Frodo puts on the Ring and the Witch-king drives a Morgul-blade into his shoulder. You leap forward with fire and sword and drive them back, but the damage is done—a shard of the blade works its way toward his heart.

---

### The Last Bridge
📍 -39.950, 176.400
📏 56000m

The Bridge of Mitheithel over the Hoarwell. Frodo grows weaker with each mile, the splinter of the Morgul-blade turning him cold. A single green beryl lies on the bridge—an elf-stone left by Glorfindel, a sign that the crossing is safe.

---

### The Trollshaws
📍 -40.400, 176.100
📏 53500m

Dense pine forest and ancient oaks. You find the three stone trolls from Bilbo's adventure, still frozen in the dawn that caught them. Even this memory cannot raise Frodo's spirits. He can barely sit upright on Bill's back.

---

### The Ford of Bruinen
📍 -40.800, 175.750
📏 10000m

Glorfindel's white horse carries Frodo alone to the ford as all nine Riders close in. 'Noro lim, Asfaloth!' The Bruinen rises in a great flood, white horses of water crashing down upon the Nazgûl. Frodo collapses on the far bank as the darkness takes him.

---

### Rivendell
📍 -40.870, 175.680

The Last Homely House east of the Sea. Elrond labors through the night to draw forth the Morgul-splinter. Frodo wakes to Gandalf's face and the sound of falling water. Here the Fellowship will be forged, and the road south decided.

---
